            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0107" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/876: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Erwin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-09T16:00:00-06:00">December 9, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:29 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>114. The Honduran Foreign Minister requests me to convey a message from the
                    President of Honduras tendering to the United States <pb facs="0108" n="98"
                        xml:id="pg98"/> Government any facilities on the Atlantic coast as well as
                    Fonseca Bay and also the use of these waters for naval bases or any other
                    purposes.</p>
                <p>The Honduran Government is communicating with the Governments of Nicaragua and El
                    Salvador requesting them to collaborate in this matter.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Managua, San Salvador and Naval Attaché.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Erwin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
